The '''Bugatti Mistral''', also called the '''Bugatti W16 Mistral''', is a [[mid-engine design|mid-engine]] two-seater sports car manufactured in [[Molsheim]], France, by French automobile manufacturer [[Bugatti Automobiles S.A.S.]] It was revealed on 19 August 2022.<ref name=":0">{{Cite web |title=Bugatti's Latest One-Off Is A 1,578-HP Tribute To The Veyron |url=https://www.motor1.com/news/785104/bugatti-fkp-hommage-one-off-specs/ |access-date=2026-01-24 |website=Motor1.com |language=en}}</ref> The Mistral is the fastest roadster in the world with a top speed achievement of 453.91 km/h (282 mph) in November 2024.<ref name=":1">{{Cite web |last=Swapnil |date=2026-01-22 |title=One-off Bugatti FKP Hommage revealed in honor of the father of the Veyron |url=https://www.thesupercarblog.com/one-off-bugatti-fkp-hommage-revealed-in-honor-of-the-father-of-the-veyron/ |access-date=2026-01-24 |website=The Supercar Blog |language=en}}</ref> Deliveries to customers began in early 2024.<ref>{{cite web |date=2022-08-24 |title=First Look: Bugatti W16 Mistral |url=https://thetrendmemo.com/first-look-bugatti-w16-mistral/ |website=thetrendmemo |access-date=2022-09-27  |archive-date=2022-09-29  |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220929150811/https://thetrendmemo.com/first-look-bugatti-w16-mistral/ |url-status=dead }}</ref> All 99 units were pre-sold at a price of €5 million.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.topgear.com/car-news/first-look/behold-eu5m-bugatti-mistral-w16-engined-speedster|title=Behold: the €5m Bugatti Mistral, a W16-engined Speedster|publisher=Top Gear|date=2022-08-19|language=en|access-date=2022-08-20}}</ref>

The Mistral is not a cabriolet version of the [[Bugatti Chiron|Chiron]] but rather a separate roadster model for Bugatti that marks the last vehicle to use the [[Bugatti W16 engine|W16 engine]] that was introduced with the [[Bugatti Veyron]] in 2005.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://ru.motor1.com/features/605536/bugatti-w16-mistral-premiere/|title=Последним Bugatti с W16 стал 1600-сильный родстер Mistral|website=Motor1.com|language=ru|date=2022-08-20}}</ref>

